# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must NOT get in matters more than what is missing. Two kinds:
#   1. ROM data in any form: the source, a generated VHDL table, a compiled simulation.
#      The source alone being excluded is not enough, what is generated from it must be
#      excluded too.
#   2. Credentials and built firmware.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- ROM data, never in the repository ---
# the folder itself is in the repository (with its README), its contents are not
roms/*
!roms/README.md
# ... also when it ends up outside roms/
*.rom
galaga*.zip
namco*.zip
# generated tables and their compiled form: make_galaga_rom.sh and build.tcl write into gen/
**/proms/*.vhd
**/work/
**/gen/
**/frames/

# --- credentials ---
# They live in sdcard/config.ini, excluded below. Nothing here uses .env files, this line is
# a precaution in case one ever appears.
*.env

# --- Gowin build output ---
impl/
*.fs
*.bin
*.bit
*.log

# --- Pico build output ---
build/
build_*/
# A built firmware carries BTstack with its non-commercial clause: redistribution only with
# the licence notice. Build output anyway, not versioned.
*.uf2
*.elf

# --- release output of scripts/make_firmware_release.sh, published on the release page ---
dist/

# --- third-party repositories under external/ ---
# FPGA-Companion, pico-sdk and tinyusb are git submodules and therefore tracked. The SDK
# caches picotool there (picotool-src), that stays untracked.
external/*
!external/FPGA-Companion
!external/pico-sdk
!external/tinyusb

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- example card: the generated file carries secrets ---
sdcard/config.ini
sdcard/galaga.ini
